00:54:12.030 --> 00:54:13.420
- Yeah, of course.

00:54:13.420 --> 00:54:18.153
Yeah so what do you make of
the claim from Arthur Smith

00:54:18.153 --> 00:54:23.153
(indistinct) crowd that Marx
is doing systematic dialectics.

00:54:24.810 --> 00:54:26.732
And how do you feel that this relates

00:54:26.732 --> 00:54:29.953
to your claims regarding domination?

00:54:32.980 --> 00:54:37.980
- Yeah, so I spent a while
as a systematic dialectitian.

00:54:46.810 --> 00:54:50.200
Around 2005, I was very into this

00:54:50.200 --> 00:54:54.110
and absolutely I think, yeah, basically

00:54:56.350 --> 00:54:59.374
I think that entire group
are engaged in a process

00:54:59.374 --> 00:55:04.374
of attempting to theoretically reconstruct

00:55:05.870 --> 00:55:09.743
the Marx's conception of capitalism.

00:55:11.700 --> 00:55:16.700
As a dialectically interrelated whole,

00:55:20.640 --> 00:55:23.273
I mean, basically to take,

00:55:25.090 --> 00:55:29.540
to save it along the lines
that Hegel's conception

00:55:29.540 --> 00:55:33.470
of absolute knowing is to historicize that

00:55:33.470 --> 00:55:36.020
and to say that's correct

00:55:36.020 --> 00:55:41.020
for the structure of capital as such.

00:55:41.030 --> 00:55:43.103
And that's that.

00:55:44.900 --> 00:55:46.980
I mean, I feel like there
are too many mediations

00:55:46.980 --> 00:55:48.450
between that and the claims

00:55:48.450 --> 00:55:50.620
that I'm making to straightforwardly say

00:55:50.620 --> 00:55:53.750
what I think the connection is there.

00:55:53.750 --> 00:55:58.640
Because in part Marie
and Rutin and Arthur,

00:55:58.640 --> 00:56:02.020
like they have a different
problematic than me.

00:56:02.020 --> 00:56:06.037
They're treating Marx
as a research program

00:56:10.100 --> 00:56:15.020
although more of a
ganglion in its character

00:56:16.437 --> 00:56:19.263
than someone like Heinrich.

00:56:24.700 --> 00:56:25.780
I think that's valuable.

00:56:25.780 --> 00:56:30.750
I think I've learned a great
deal about Marx's texts

00:56:30.750 --> 00:56:35.113
from those guys, but it always seems to me

00:56:38.580 --> 00:56:41.713
to be a fundamentally fighting,

00:56:43.690 --> 00:56:47.830
still fighting off the Ricardians.

00:56:47.830 --> 00:56:52.740
The Ricardian Marxists, still
doing that sort of thing.

00:56:52.740 --> 00:56:55.830
And that's all great, and
I'm totally on their side

00:56:55.830 --> 00:56:59.070
on that fight, but I don't think

00:56:59.070 --> 00:57:04.070
it has an immediate
relationship to anything

00:57:04.577 --> 00:57:07.330
like the political payoff

00:57:07.330 --> 00:57:12.330
or the political intervention of capital.

00:57:13.810 --> 00:57:16.570
And so I'm not really sure.

00:57:16.570 --> 00:57:18.400
And you can see that in the bracketing

00:57:18.400 --> 00:57:20.800
of the historical material when they try

00:57:20.800 --> 00:57:23.400
to reconstruct "Capital"
along those lines, I think.

00:57:26.710 --> 00:57:29.970
- Okay, Paul's system
is apparently crashed.

