00:58:11.030 --> 00:58:13.440
and like being open to
the way that other people

00:58:13.440 --> 00:58:17.830
approach Marx, I'm unclear
on what you're trying to say

00:58:17.830 --> 00:58:21.470
about how critique functions in Marx

00:58:21.470 --> 00:58:23.970
because of what I think that means.

00:58:23.970 --> 00:58:28.970
I agree that if, like I
understand what you were saying

00:58:30.290 --> 00:58:33.483
by like a political critique of Science,

00:58:35.180 --> 00:58:37.200
it's probably better characterized

00:58:37.200 --> 00:58:40.930
than that by I forget what
you can try say that again

00:58:40.930 --> 00:58:43.008
like the producing enlightenment

00:58:43.008 --> 00:58:45.713
and then shedding off ideology,

00:58:47.080 --> 00:58:51.876
but I've always linked
critique to like this,

00:58:51.876 --> 00:58:56.876
like thing that happens beginning with con

00:58:58.000 --> 00:58:59.033
that I see.

00:59:00.030 --> 00:59:03.960
Because I'm approaching Marx
more from like a philosophical

00:59:03.960 --> 00:59:08.540
background where like the
like appropriate dualidic

00:59:08.540 --> 00:59:12.563
gets like centered in
philosophical method.

00:59:14.560 --> 00:59:17.310
So, yeah and I would, I would
agree that I've really paid

00:59:17.310 --> 00:59:20.430
attention to like,
Marx's the popularization

00:59:20.430 --> 00:59:25.110
of marches language like the
language in the Grundrisse

00:59:25.110 --> 00:59:29.283
and contribution to political economy.

00:59:30.870 --> 00:59:35.770
He's talking about all like
universal this, particular that

00:59:35.770 --> 00:59:40.770
like every other category, it seems to,

00:59:43.410 --> 00:59:46.730
the I forget if the language
is like that in "Capital".

00:59:46.730 --> 00:59:50.310
But and alienation is
still a category used

00:59:50.310 --> 00:59:51.583
in those texts too.

00:59:54.430 --> 00:59:58.003
So, yeah, I don't know if
what I'm saying is clear.

01:00:00.160 --> 01:00:01.980
- Well, I mean, you raised a few issues.

01:00:01.980 --> 01:00:03.730
so I don't know that
I'll get to all of them

01:00:03.730 --> 01:00:08.730
but I do think that connection
to the history of critique

01:00:10.350 --> 01:00:11.880
and the way the different ways

01:00:11.880 --> 01:00:16.880
in which critique gets used
to entitle different projects.

01:00:19.030 --> 01:00:20.760
I mean, I think that's an interesting

01:00:20.760 --> 01:00:23.410
and a storied question.

01:00:23.410 --> 01:00:27.340
One that I wouldn't be
able to do great justice to

01:00:27.340 --> 01:00:30.350
but I do think there's a
fairly straightforward way

01:00:30.350 --> 01:00:33.760
in which I think the
critique of political economy

01:00:33.760 --> 01:00:37.490
is a critique in a sense
that con could recognize,

01:00:37.490 --> 01:00:42.490
which is that, part of what a critique,

01:00:42.499 --> 01:00:45.063
what the critique of pure reason does,

01:00:46.130 --> 01:00:50.680
what it does is it finds the
proper domain of pure reason

01:00:50.680 --> 01:00:52.980
that defines it.

01:00:52.980 --> 01:00:55.820
It finds the polices where the limits

01:00:55.820 --> 01:01:00.063
beyond which if it goes,
it produces monsters.

01:01:01.120 --> 01:01:04.870
So in some important sense
that's what Marx is doing as well

01:01:04.870 --> 01:01:06.940
with the critical political economy

01:01:06.940 --> 01:01:10.820
and that he's trying to
define political economy.

01:01:10.820 --> 01:01:14.840
And that means to delimit
it right, to find its limits

01:01:14.840 --> 01:01:18.233
to find the points beyond
which it cannot go.

01:01:20.550 --> 01:01:23.980
And in that sense to relativize it,

01:01:23.980 --> 01:01:28.980
to locate it in the sphere
of history and knowledge.

01:01:32.470 --> 01:01:34.770
So I think that's fairly,

01:01:34.770 --> 01:01:36.300
I think you can say that

01:01:36.300 --> 01:01:39.173
and I don't think that's
super controversial.

01:01:40.840 --> 01:01:42.623
Yeah, I'll stop there.

