So I'll just read it,

01:06:10.222 --> 01:06:13.613
and the question is that
the the Russian translation

01:06:16.180 --> 01:06:20.170
is important Marx thought highly of it.

01:06:20.170 --> 01:06:25.170
And so why bring the French translation

01:06:25.980 --> 01:06:30.875
so much into play and not give
the same kind of attention

01:06:30.875 --> 01:06:33.280
extrapolating a little bit

01:06:33.280 --> 01:06:35.780
to the to the Russian translation.

01:06:35.780 --> 01:06:37.170
And Will, I know you've thought a lot

01:06:37.170 --> 01:06:38.490
about the French translation.

01:06:38.490 --> 01:06:40.890
I mentioned that in the introduction,

01:06:40.890 --> 01:06:44.230
I mean the obvious answer I
suppose is that Marx basically

01:06:44.230 --> 01:06:46.170
did much of a French translation himself.

01:06:46.170 --> 01:06:49.910
And so, there are parts of
it that function essentially

01:06:49.910 --> 01:06:53.030
as commentary on his work.

01:06:53.030 --> 01:06:56.590
He also, as we know how
to somewhat low opinion

01:06:56.590 --> 01:07:00.584
of the French intellectually,

01:07:00.584 --> 01:07:05.584
maybe, I mean, in his exchange
with angles of well-known

01:07:05.830 --> 01:07:08.862
exchange about the punch translation,

01:07:08.862 --> 01:07:12.316
he recycled some old German tropes

01:07:12.316 --> 01:07:16.750
about French culture and its
